  "checks": [
    "The actual state and scalar energy bounds each select their own parameterLoss at fixed arity n+1, before all output orders and radius selectors. The genuine existing interpolation lemma is applied with oldLoss=loss+parameterLoss.",
    "The state low/high angular-material budgets and the scalar physical-height budgets are preserved. Nat.add_assoc is explicit where their source notation meets the interpolation interface.",
    "The finite sum over CircleJetIndex s is retained. Constants for b/c are summed only over the actual finite square or jet-index set for that s; there is no infinite supremum over derivative arities.",
    "The cyclic-slot wrapper is specialized to a supplied n; its mathematical rotation and same actual field stay unchanged. All three preceding generic private proofs remain byte-identical.",
    "The same actual multilinear circle realization is split into pure scalar and state-slot terms. Only the two finite values B_state/B_scalar and L_state/L_scalar are combined, after n is fixed. Generic projections, multilinear telescoping and reference grading proofs remain byte-identical.",
    "Homogeneous normalization uses the same algebraic multilinear map and genuine circle decoder. The final sharp one-high expression and positive product bound on a low-order box remain actual estimates for those fields.",
    "All quantitative public statements move n before the existential low-order/loss pair. The box-product statement likewise takes n before B and only quantifies over s afterward. No common all-arity neighborhood/order is asserted."
  ],
